{"name":"Dreamland","hex":"#b5b1bf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dreamland","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Area 51 military base in Nevada, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dreamland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dreamland (manfra)","blocks":[{"text":"Dreamland is a French comic book (manfra) series written and illustrated by Reno Lemaire. The series has been published by Pika Édition since January 2006 and has 24 volumes released in French as of July 2026. It was later published by the Japanese publisher Euromanga and Asukashinsha in October 2024. An animated television series adaptation produced by Ellipse Animation and La Chouette Compagnie is set to premiere in France and Japan in October 2026, with Animation Digital Network and Crunchyroll streaming the series."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d6/Dreamland_manfra_volume_1_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamland_(manfra)","wikidata":"Q3039286"},{"title":"Dreamland (2006 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Dreamland is an American drama film that was released on December 19, 2006. The primary plot focuses concern overcoming fear, struggling friend to friend relationships, and overall coming of age in small-town America."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Dreamland2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamland_(2006_film)","wikidata":"Q1428139"},{"title":"Dreamland (Glass Animals album)","blocks":[{"text":"Dreamland is the third studio album by English indie rock band Glass Animals. It was released on 7 August 2020, having been pushed back from its initial release date of 10 July 2020."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/Dreamland_%28Glass_Animals%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamland_(Glass_Animals_album)","wikidata":"Q98279558"},{"title":"Dreamland (Coney Island, 1904)","blocks":[{"text":"Dreamland was an amusement park that operated in the Coney Island neighborhood of Brooklyn in New York City, United States, from 1904 to 1911. It was the last of the three original large parks built on Coney Island, along with Steeplechase Park and Luna Park. The park was between Surf Avenue to the north and the Atlantic Ocean to the south. It was arranged roughly as a horseshoe, with a pier facing south toward the Atlantic Ocean. Dreamland contained several attractions that were larger versions of those at Luna Park, and it included a human zoo, several early roller coasters, a Shoot the Chutes ride, and a replica of Venice. Dreamland also hosted entertainment and dramatic spectacles based on morality themes. Several structures, such as the Pompeiian, Electricity, and Submarine Boat buildings, were dedicated to exhibits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Dreamland_Park%2C_1905.JPG/330px-Dreamland_Park%2C_1905.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamland_(Coney_Island%2C_1904)","wikidata":"Q3039284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Dave_Studio_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Dave_Studio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Dave_Studio_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Dave_Studio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Dave_Studio_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Dave_Studio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADave_Studio_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Joe_Seaward%2C_Glass_Animals%2C_The_Riverside_Theater%2C_Milwaukee%2C_WI%2C_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Joe_Seaward%2C_Glass_Animals%2C_The_Riverside_Theater%2C_Milwaukee%2C_WI%2C_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Joe_Seaward%2C_Glass_Animals%2C_The_Riverside_Theater%2C_Milwaukee%2C_WI%2C_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Joe_Seaward%2C_Glass_Animals%2C_The_Riverside_Theater%2C_Milwaukee%2C_WI%2C_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Joe_Seaward%2C_Glass_Animals%2C_The_Riverside_Theater%2C_Milwaukee%2C_WI%2C_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Joe_Seaward%2C_Glass_Animals%2C_The_Riverside_Theater%2C_Milwaukee%2C_WI%2C_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoe_Seaward%2C_Glass_Animals%2C_The_Riverside_Theater%2C_Milwaukee%2C_WI%2C_2015_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Streetfighter1.jpg/500px-Streetfighter1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Streetfighter1.jpg/1280px-Streetfighter1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Streetfighter1.jpg/500px-Streetfighter1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStreetfighter1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Dr._Dre_in_2011.jpg/120px-Dr._Dre_in_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://uplo